endobj
537 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We will create Anime Profiles by applying One-Hot Encoding to these categorical features. This encoding helps convert each feature into a numerical vector, allowing us to represent each anime in a multi-dimensional feature space. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
538 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Step 2: Building User Profiles)
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
539 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To create User Profiles, we will sum up the anime profile vectors for all the anime a user has watched and multiply each anime vector by the rating given by the user to weigh their preferences. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This process ensures that the user's profile captures their preferences based on the types of anime they watch and their ratings. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
